tariq: Heads-up from a customer run: after an auth refresh we saw duplicate side-effects when a 429 hit immediately. This was with the Rust SDK prototype and Node.
ana: Interesting — Rust SDK is new here. Is the body rewindable? That often explains the replay.
tariq: No, the request body is a streaming reader; the Rust client attempted a replay without a saved idempotency token.
leah: Core ask: we need a cross-SDK rule: do not auto-retry mutating requests across token refresh unless a retry-safe marker is present (Idempotency-Key or explicit opt-in). Also, require honoring Retry-After when present.
nana: Agreed. Suggested defaults for 429s: base=60ms, multiplier=2, cap=1800ms, full jitter. If Retry-After exists, convert to ms and use max(Retry-After, computedBackoff) up to 5s cap.
tariq: For streaming bodies, the SDK should either buffer/rewind or refuse to auto-retry and surface a clear error or opt-in config. Rust SDK will default to "no auto-replay for streaming bodies" and expose a `allow_stream_replay` flag (false by default).
leah: Add to sample-app: an example middleware that attaches an idempotency token to POSTs and a token-refresh hook that serializes mutating calls during refresh. Small code snippet we want in sample app: 
```
// pseudo-js middleware
app.use(async (req, next) => {
  if (req.method === 'POST' && !req.headers['Idempotency-Key']) {
    req.headers['Idempotency-Key'] = uuid();
  }
  return next();
});
```
nana: Also propose a short SDK parity test: simulate 401 -> refresh -> 429 with no Retry-After and assert no duplicate side-effects if no idempotency key. If idempotency key present, replay is allowed and should succeed.
tariq: Can we add telemetry tags when a replay happens across refresh so we can alert quickly? e.g., tag: replay_across_refresh=true, body_rewound=true/false.
leah: Yes. Add metric: sdk.replay_across_refresh.count and sample-app CI should fail if any test without idempotency key causes a replay.
devx-ci: New test job added: sdk-replay-parity (runs Node/Python/Go/Rust).
ops-bot: Alert rule created: replay_across_refresh.rate > 0.2% -> ticket #1402.
tariq: I'll open: 1) sample-app PR with middleware + CI test, 2) Rust SDK change with allow_stream_replay flag + telemetry. Assign @ana @leah for review.
nana: I'll draft a one-page RFC for parity (Node/Python/Go/Rust) outlining: auth-refresh ordering, streaming body policy, default 429 jitter, Retry-After handling, and telemetry. Keep it short.
leah: Great. Once RFC lands, update onboarding quickstart with a short note about idempotency for mutating endpoints.
tariq: Thanks everyone :thumbsup:
